<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Contact patch test across NON-MATCHING interface meshes (3D, mortar segmentation)</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>yes</isVerified>
    <description>
      The 3D counterpart of ContactMortarPatch2d, and the only testcase that reaches the POLYGON
      CLIPPING branch of the mortar segmentation. The 2D tests exercise only its interval
      branch, where a cut is a break point on a line; here a secondary element is clipped
      against a projected primary quadrilateral in both surface directions, and what survives is
      fan-triangulated.

      The lower body has a 3x3 interface mesh, the upper a 2x2, so every one of the four
      secondary elements straddles primary boundaries in BOTH directions and its clip polygon is
      a genuine sub-rectangle rather than the whole element. That is the smallest configuration
      in which the clipping actually does something.

      As in 2D the Poisson ratio is zero, so the exact solution is uniform uniaxial stress and
      the exact contact pressure is the applied 1e6 Pa everywhere, independent of the mesh.

      maxPressure = 1e6 exact only WITH mortar segmentation totalContactForce = 4e6 applied
      pressure x area; exact either way, by equilibrium numCells > numSegments the fingerprint
      that clipping happened at all
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactMortarPatch3d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="3d">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="3d">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="mortar_patch3d"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       segmentation="mortar"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body fully supported -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/><comp dof="z"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- upper body: suppress the two lateral rigid-body modes only. Its z support
               comes exclusively from the contact interface. -->
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
